              <strong>Focus:</strong> Autoregulated mastery, peak functional conditioning, and 1-year transformation testing.
            </div>
            <p class="month-bio-adaptation">
              <strong>Biological Adaptations:</strong> High bone mineral density, resting heart rate under 60 bpm, testosterone optimization, and an unbreakable physical habit embedded for decades of longevity.
            </p>
          </div>
          <button class="btn-jump-month" onclick="jumpToMonthDay(301)">▶ Jump to Day 301</button>
        </div>
      </div>

    </main>
  </div>

  <!-- ==========================================
       VIEW 3: GYM ESSENTIALS & LIFESTYLE HANDBOOK
       ========================================== -->
  <div id="essentialsView" class="app-view">
    <main class="container">
      
      <div class="pro-section-card">
        <div class="pro-section-head">
          <h2>🎒 Everything Else Required While Doing Gym (The Unwritten Rules)</h2>
          <p>Proper workout execution requires the right footwear, breathing mechanics, recovery environment, and mindset.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="essentials-grid">
          
          <div class="essential-box">
            <h3>👟 1. Footwear: Why Running Shoes Destroy Knee Angles</h3>
            <p>
              The most dangerous mistake beginners make is squatting or lunging in cushioned running shoes (Nike Air, Boost foam). Thick foam acts like an unstable marshmallow under load, causing your ankles to pronate and knees to cave inward.
            </p>
            <div class="dos-donts-grid">
              <div class="do-col">
                <strong>✓ WEAR THIS:</strong><br>
                • Barefoot / Grip Socks<br>
                • Flat shoes (Converse Chucks, Vans)<br>
                • Minimalist / Barefoot trainers
              </div>
              <div class="dont-col">
                <strong>✗ AVOID THIS:</strong><br>
                • Thick running sneakers<br>
                • Cushioned air/gel soles<br>
                • Slippery smooth socks
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="essential-box">
            <h3>🫁 2. The Valsalva Maneuver (Spine Protection Breathing)</h3>
            <p>
              Improper breathing causes dizziness and leaves your lower back unprotected. Follow this 3-step breathing cycle:
            </p>
            <ul style="margin: 10px 0 0 16px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6;">
              <li><strong>Step 1 (Before Descent):</strong> Inhale deeply into your belly (360° diaphragmatic expansion), not into your chest.</li>
              <li><strong>Step 2 (During Descent):</strong> Hold your breath and brace your abdominal wall as if preparing to take a punch. This creates high intra-abdominal pressure (IAP) that acts as an internal weightlifting belt.</li>
              <li><strong>Step 3 (Past Sticking Point):</strong> Exhale forcefully through pursed lips only after you pass the hardest point of the ascent.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="essential-box">
            <h3>⚠️ 3. Muscle Soreness (DOMS) vs. Injury Pain: How to Tell</h3>
            <p>
              Learn the difference between healthy adaptation and dangerous tissue damage:
            </p>
            <div class="dos-donts-grid">
              <div class="do-col">
                <strong>GOOD SORENESS (DOMS):</strong><br>
                • Dull, aching fullness in muscle belly<br>
                • Peaks 24–48 hours after workout<br>
                • Improves after warm-up & walking
              </div>
              <div class="dont-col">
                <strong>DANGER PAIN (STOP!):</strong><br>
                • Sharp, stabbing or pinch sensation<br>
                • Located directly in knee/shoulder joint<br>
                • Sharp pain that worsens with reps
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="essential-box">
            <h3>🏠 4. Living Room Gym Setup for a 6'0" Male</h3>
            <p>
              Being 6 feet tall requires specific environmental safety measures:
            </p>
            <ul style="margin: 10px 0 0 16px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6;">
              <li><strong>Ceiling Clearance Check:</strong> Stand tall and reach overhead with straight arms. Ensure ceiling fans and lights are well out of reach before Month 3's pull-up bar arrives.</li>
              <li><strong>Surface Grip:</strong> Workout on a wooden/tile floor with a high-density 6mm–8mm exercise mat to protect tailbone during dead bugs and glute bridges.</li>
              <li><strong>Airflow & Ventilation:</strong> Keep a fan or open window nearby. Dehydration and overheating spike heart rate unnecessarily on long sets.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="essential-box">
            <h3>🌙 5. Sleep & Hormonal Recovery for Men at 35</h3>
            <p>
              At 35, testosterone naturally declines by 1% per year if recovery is neglected. 70% of growth hormone release occurs during deep slow-wave sleep:
            </p>
            <ul style="margin: 10px 0 0 16px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6;">
              <li><strong>Target 7.5 to 8.5 Hours:</strong> Sleeping 5–6 hours drops daytime testosterone by 15% and elevates catabolic cortisol.</li>
              <li><strong>Cool Dark Room (19°C / 66°F):</strong> Lowers body core temperature for faster sleep onset.</li>
              <li><strong>Zero Blue Light 45 mins before bed:</strong> Allows melatonin to surge naturally.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="essential-box">
            <h3>👕 6. Workout Clothing & Grip Essentials</h3>
            <p>
              What you wear directly affects your range of motion:
            </p>
            <ul style="margin: 10px 0 0 16px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6;">
              <li><strong>Shorts:</strong> Wear athletic shorts with stretch that do NOT catch or bind on your knees when reaching deep 90° squats.</li>
              <li><strong>Sweat Towel:</strong> Keep a microfiber hand towel to wipe palms and maintain grip on doorframe rows and pushup surfaces.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

    </main>
  </div>

  <!-- FLOATING REST STOPWATCH WIDGET -->
  <div class="floating-timer">
    <div>
      <div style="font-size: 0.7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; color: var(--text-muted);">Rest Timer</div>
      <div class="timer-digits" id="timerDigits">01:00</div>
    </div>
    <div class="timer-actions">
      <button class="t-btn" onclick="startTimer(45)">45s</button>
      <button class="t-btn" onclick="startTimer(60)">60s</button>
      <button class="t-btn" onclick="startTimer(90)">90s</button>
      <button class="t-btn" style="background: rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.2); border-color: rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.4);" onclick="resetTimer()">Reset</button>
    </div>
  </div>

